& [Purpose]
  + form the first provider-free identity envelope for the slim outer Cantor that will later host a model and launch an inner Cantor
  + keep declared identity distinct from physical observation loading launch inference attention negotiation and effect authority

& [Profiles]
  + [NHO-001] request profile is cantor-nested-outer-host-identity-request/0.1
  + [NHO-002] envelope profile is cantor-nested-outer-host-identity-envelope/0.1
  + [NHO-003] all machine forms deny unknown fields and use deterministic JSON over closed typed values

& [OuterProcessBinding]
  + [NHO-004] session host process and outer-model identities are four distinct SemanticId values
  + [NHO-005] the process binding carries outer-host kind declared-unobserved state implementation SHA256 configuration SHA256 and bounded supervisor profile
  + [NHO-006] declared-unobserved is the only P0 process state and cannot imply PID start time executable path listener readiness or physical liveness

& [OuterModelBinding]
  + [NHO-007] the outer model binding carries selector role declared-unloaded state provider family model selector model artifact runtime and configuration SHA256 identities
  + [NHO-008] declared-unloaded is the only P0 model state and cannot imply model availability loading inference quality ownership or provider contact

& [SessionBounds]
  + [NHO-009] maximum inner processes is exactly one and maximum model instances is exactly two as future composition ceilings only
  + [NHO-010] attention frame bytes are within one through 33554432 iterations within one through 64 and timeout seconds within one through 86400
  + [NHO-011] one through 32 evidence references are required and unresolved account is exactly physical_process_not_observed model_not_loaded and provider_not_contacted

& [Envelope]
  + [NHO-012] compilation validates the request then emits proposed-identity-only lifecycle identity-only authority exact fixed capability denials and the complete unchanged request
  + [NHO-013] request and envelope digests are domain-separated SHA256 over deterministic JSON with only the target digest blanked
  + [NHO-014] validation rederives request semantics request digest envelope digest lifecycle authority denials and exact request correspondence

& [CapabilityDenials]
  + [NHO-015] exact denials are process launch model load provider call persistence external effect and remote access
  + [NHO-016] nonauthority is one fixed string and no field grants inner identity launch model custody shared attention or product authority

& [Faults]
  + [NHO-017] invalid profile identity collision digest text process binding model binding bounds evidence unresolved authority lifecycle correspondence and machine form fail closed with typed faults
  + [NHO-018] any envelope mutation or request substitution refuses without partial output

& [Acceptance]
  + [NHO-A01] source manifest canonical exploded SJS review plan matrix phase lock and signature bind exactly
  + [NHO-A02] valid fixture compiles validates serializes round-trips and byte-identically replays
  + [NHO-A03] unknown fields identity collisions state widening malformed digests empty evidence wrong unresolved account and every bound substitution refuse
  + [NHO-A04] request output denial lifecycle authority and digest tampering refuse
  + [NHO-A05] focused debug overflow-checked release warnings-denied lint format workspace regression evidence attribution and scoped Git gates pass

& [Delineation]
  + this envelope identifies a proposed outer session host process claim and unloaded model claim
  + it is not a process observation supervisor command provider configuration model loader launch plan inner-host identity shared-attention frame or agent execution

& [AuthorityBoundary]
  + permits pure Rust forms validation deterministic digest compilation tests fixtures documentation proof and evidence only
  + excludes filesystem process environment clock network provider model loading inference MCP persistence signing installation deployment external effect remote FPGA and Minecraft actions

